{"created": "2026-06-08T04:32:01.712091+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-08T04:32:02.122711+00:00", "id": 20587698, "conceptrecid": "20587697", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20587697", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "metadata": {"title": "Self-Model as Social Decoupler: Ablation and Baseline Evidence for Reflective Mediation in Proto-Conscious Agents", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "publication_date": "2026-06-08", "description": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>The PROSENTIR series investigates the computational correlates of proto-consciousness through agent-based simulations of iterative cooperation. Paper 6 addresses a central open question from Papers 4 and 5: does the self-model mechanism causally produce the internal autonomy indexed by C, or does it merely correlate with it? We report three independent empirical modules. Module C validates mutual information estimators: MINE-SMILE diverges systematically (&Delta; mean &asymp; 56) on emergent differential-of-sigmoid distributions, while the Kraskov k-NN estimator remains stable (&Phi;\u209a = 2.19), ratifying Kraskov as the canonical estimator for the PROSENTIR series with empirical rather than conventional justification. Module A ablates the self-model (w\u209b = 0, N = 200 pairs per condition): the self-model suppresses the synchrony-cooperation coupling from r = 0.478 to r = 0.029 (p &lt; 0.0001), confirming H6.1, and introduces cooperative behavioral variance (&sigma; = 0.151 vs. 0.062 without self-model). Module B compares PROSENTIR against three baselines (RNN, Tit-for-Tat, Memory agent, N = 200 each): all systems without self-model show synchrony-cooperation coupling r &ge; 0.478; only PROSENTIR with self-model collapses that effect. Additionally, the autonomy-cooperation trade-off present in all baselines (r = &minus;0.551 to &minus;0.606) is neutralized in PROSENTIR (r = &minus;0.045). We interpret these results as computational evidence for the saber-que / saber-desde distinction formalized in Paper 3: without the self-model, agents act as social mirrors; with it, they exhibit reflexive mediation of social responses. The cost of this mediation is social desynchronization; the benefit is behavioral stability and trade-off neutralization.</span></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Santoyo Ortiz, Armando", "affiliation": "Idependent Research", "orcid": "0009-0004-0904-9131"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Santoyo Ortiz, Armando", "affiliation": "independent research", "type": "Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0004-0904-9131"}], "keywords": ["proto-consciousness, self-model, mutual information, Tit-for-Tat, ablation study, saber-desde, PROSENTIR, agent-based simulation, cooperative behavior"], "dates": [{"type": "submitted"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20587697"}}]}}, "title": "Self-Model as Social Decoupler: Ablation and Baseline Evidence for Reflective Mediation in Proto-Conscious Agents", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20587698", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20587698?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20587698", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587697", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20587697", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20587697", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20587697", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20587698:PROSENTIR_Paper6_ES.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20587698/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20587698/requests"}, "updated": "2026-06-08T04:32:02.122711+00:00", "recid": "20587698", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "a808fa1e-8c1e-4128-afe0-8205e257385d", "key": "PRO